# Python virtual environment

All Python tooling in this repo runs inside **`.venv`**. Never install packages globally or use system `pip`/`python3` for project work.

## Setup

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
ansible-galaxy collection install -r collections/requirements.yml -p collections
```

## Commands

Always activate the venv first (or call `.venv/bin/python` / `.venv/bin/pip` explicitly):

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
ansible-navigator run playbooks/contain_runtime_violation.yml ...
ansible-playbook playbooks/contain_runtime_violation.yml ...
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Agent expectations

- Run `pip install`, `ansible-playbook`, `ansible-navigator`, and `ansible-builder` only with the venv active.
- Prefer `.venv/bin/<tool>` in scripts when activation is awkward.
- Do not add `sudo pip install` or modify system site-packages.
- After changing `requirements.txt`, reinstall in `.venv` and rebuild the EE if dependencies affect the execution environment.
- Playbooks use `VIRTUAL_ENV` for `ansible_python_interpreter` when the venv is active.
